{"type":"lesson.started","request_id":"78021543-2925-4d3b-ae41-21f4ad41e36f","title":"The normal distribution and the 68-95-99.7 rule"}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"78021543-2925-4d3b-ae41-21f4ad41e36f","step":{"id":"s1","script":"A normal distribution is symmetric about its mean. Measuring distance in standard deviations gives the same bell curve for every normal distribution.","ops":[{"op":"text","id":"title","region":"A1","content":"The 68–95–99.7 rule"},{"op":"equation","id":"standardize","anchor":{"el":"title","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"Z=\\frac{X-\\mu}{\\sigma},\\qquad \\mu=\\text{mean},\\quad \\sigma=\\text{standard deviation}"},{"op":"figure","id":"bell","region":"right","frame":{"x":[-3.6,3.6],"y":[-0.025,0.45],"axes":"edge","x_label":"Standard deviations, z","y_label":"Probability density"},"marks":[{"kind":"fn","id":"normal","y":"exp(-x^2/2)/sqrt(2*pi)","domain":[-3.6,3.6]},{"kind":"segment","id":"centerline","from":[0,0],"to":{"on":"normal","x":0},"stroke":"dashed"},{"kind":"point","at":[0,0],"label":"0"}]}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"78021543-2925-4d3b-ae41-21f4ad41e36f","step":{"id":"s2","script":"Probability is area under the curve. About 68 percent lies within one standard deviation of the mean, between minus one and plus one.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"one_sigma","on":"bell","marks":[{"kind":"shade","under":"normal","from":-1,"to":1},{"kind":"segment","from":[-1,0],"to":{"on":"normal","x":-1},"stroke":"dashed"},{"kind":"segment","from":[1,0],"to":{"on":"normal","x":1},"stroke":"dashed"},{"kind":"point","at":[-1,0],"label":"−1"},{"kind":"point","at":[1,0],"label":"+1"},{"kind":"text","at":[0,0.14],"text":"68%"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"rule68","anchor":{"el":"standardize","side":"below","gap":0.1},"latex":"P(\\mu-\\sigma\\le X\\le\\mu+\\sigma)\\approx68\\%"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"78021543-2925-4d3b-ae41-21f4ad41e36f","step":{"id":"s3","script":"Extend the interval to two standard deviations on each side. The accumulated area is about 95 percent, leaving about 5 percent outside.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"two_sigma","on":"bell","marks":[{"kind":"shade","under":"normal","from":-2,"to":-1},{"kind":"shade","under":"normal","from":1,"to":2},{"kind":"segment","from":[-2,0],"to":{"on":"normal","x":-2},"stroke":"dashed"},{"kind":"segment","from":[2,0],"to":{"on":"normal","x":2},"stroke":"dashed"},{"kind":"point","at":[-2,0],"label":"−2"},{"kind":"point","at":[2,0],"label":"+2"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"rule95","anchor":{"el":"rule68","side":"below","gap":0.1},"latex":"P(\\mu-2\\sigma\\le X\\le\\mu+2\\sigma)\\approx95\\%"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"78021543-2925-4d3b-ae41-21f4ad41e36f","step":{"id":"s4","script":"Within three standard deviations lies about 99.7 percent. Only 0.3 percent remains outside, split equally between the two tails.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"three_sigma","on":"bell","marks":[{"kind":"shade","under":"normal","from":-3,"to":-2},{"kind":"shade","under":"normal","from":2,"to":3},{"kind":"segment","from":[-3,0],"to":{"on":"normal","x":-3},"stroke":"dashed"},{"kind":"segment","from":[3,0],"to":{"on":"normal","x":3},"stroke":"dashed"},{"kind":"point","at":[-3,0],"label":"−3"},{"kind":"point","at":[3,0],"label":"+3"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"rule997","anchor":{"el":"rule95","side":"below","gap":0.1},"latex":"P(\\mu-3\\sigma\\le X\\le\\mu+3\\sigma)\\approx99.7\\%"},{"op":"equation","id":"tails","anchor":{"el":"rule997","side":"below","gap":0.06},"latex":"\\text{Each outer tail}\\approx\\frac{0.3\\%}{2}=0.15\\%"}],"checkpoint":{"question":"About what percentage lies outside two standard deviations of the mean?","expected_gist":"5% total, or 2.5% in each tail."}}}
